{"name":"Barite","hex":"#9e7b5c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral, barium sulphate, with the chemical formula BaSO4."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baryte","blocks":[{"text":"Baryte or barite ( BARR-eyet, BAIR-), also called barytes ( bə-RY-teez), is a mineral consisting of barium sulfate (BaSO4). Baryte is generally white or colorless, and is the main source of the element barium. The baryte group consists of baryte, celestine (strontium sulfate), anglesite (lead sulfate), and anhydrite (calcium sulfate). Baryte and celestine form a solid solution (Ba,Sr)SO4."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Barite_-_Cerro_Warihuyn%2C_Miraflores%2C_Huamalies%2C_Huanuco%2C_Peru.jpg/330px-Barite_-_Cerro_Warihuyn%2C_Miraflores%2C_Huamalies%2C_Huanuco%2C_Peru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baryte"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Barite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png/500px-Barite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Barite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png/500px-Barite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The unit cell of baryte","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barite_FRIZINGTON.jpg/500px-Barite_FRIZINGTON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Barite_FRIZINGTON.jpg/1280px-Barite_FRIZINGTON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t